---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---

<Base>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <section class="text-center">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Atlas</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text">
        Your personal news agent.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-text-muted">
        Connect your sources — GitHub, arXiv, RSS, HN, Reddit, Telegram. Atlas tells you what changed,
        what it means for <em class="text-text not-italic font-medium">your stack</em>, and what to do next.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-10 flex items-center justify-center gap-4">
        <a
          href="/signup"
          class="rounded-lg bg-primary px-6 py-3 text-base font-semibold text-white transition-colors hover:bg-primary-hover"
        >
          Get started
        </a>
        <a href="/docs" class="text-base font-medium text-text-muted hover:text-text">
          How it works →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-24 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface p-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">Per-user scoring</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-muted">
          Every item scored against your profile, not the crowd. 5 items that matter to you beat 30 that don't.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface p-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">Impact reasoning</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-muted">
          A reasoning model answers: does this affect your stack? what should you do? confidence level?
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface p-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">Compounds</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-muted">
          Feedback refines your profile. The more you use Atlas, the sharper it gets. No competitor can replicate you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-24 rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface-2 p-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text">Why not Hacker News or daily.dev?</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
        They solve overload for the crowd. Atlas solves it for you. HN gives 30 stories for everyone;
        Atlas gives you 5 for your work. daily.dev personalizes by click; Atlas personalizes by
        impact on your actual stack.
      </p>
    </section>

    <footer class="mt-24 border-t border-border pt-8 text-sm text-text-muted">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <span>AGPL-3.0 · <a href="https://github.com/pantha704/atlas">GitHub</a></span>
        <span>v0.1 — in active development</span>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Base>
